From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:38:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 239/342] meson_encoder: a bit rate, by a rate control of its
 own

The S905's encoder has no rate control of its own on GXBB: the caller
picks a QP for each picture. With a bit rate asked for (encode_parameters'
avg_field_size, bytes a picture), the plugin now picks it: the P
pictures' QP follows a model of their size (it halves every 6 steps,
from the last pictures' sizes) toward the average less a share of what
was written beyond it, so that IDR pictures and busy scenes are made up
within half a second; an IDR picture takes 3 below, but no lower than
keeps it within half the driver's 1 MB bitstream buffer. QP 14 to 51.
Without a bit rate, the quality's QP as before. A line in the log at the
end says what was asked, what was written and the QPs used.

The FFmpeg plugin's encoder takes a video bit rate from avg_field_size
too (it was a TODO): MPEG-4 clips, without the hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
